b $EF9C Display Record
D $EF9C Display record read by #R$C9BF. The show-message command at #R$EE95 passes this word to
. #R$C591.
N $EF9C Named from the script command at #R$EE95.
B $EF9C,$02 Display record read by #R$C9BF: flags #N$00, value #N$00.

c $EF9E Set The Print Flag And Print
@ $EF9E label=SetPrintFlagAndPrint
D $EF9E Sets the print flag, prints the message in hand, and marks success.
N $EF9E Run by #R$CA64 after the display record at #R$EF9C, from the show-message command at #R$EE95.
  $EF9E,$03 Take the message at #R$75D2+#N$16.
  $EFA1,$05 Set the print flag (#SKOOLKID$5C3C(TV_FLAG)).
  $EFA6,$03 Call #R$A59F to print the message.
  $EFA9,$02,b$01 Reset the zero flag.
  $EFAB,$01 Return.

b $EFAC Display Record
D $EFAC Display record read by #R$C9BF. The show-message command at #R$EF01 passes this word to
. #R$C591.
N $EFAC Named from the script command at #R$EF01.
B $EFAC,$02 Display record read by #R$C9BF: flags #N$00, value #N$00.

c $EFAE Print This Handler's Message
@ $EFAE label=PrintHandlerMessage
D $EFAE Prints the message at #R$75D2+#N$31.
N $EFAE Run by #R$CA64 after the display record at #R$EFAC, from the show-message command at #R$EF01.
  $EFAE,$05 Take the message at #R$75D2+#N$31 and go to #R$EFA1 to print it.

b $EFB3 Display Record
D $EFB3 Display record read by #R$C9BF. The show-message commands at #R$EE3D and #R$EEBB pass
. this word to #R$C591.
N $EFB3 Named from the script commands at #R$EE3D and #R$EEBB.
B $EFB3,$02 Display record read by #R$C9BF: flags #N$00, value #N$00.

c $EFB5 Store The Character's Text Pointer
@ $EFB5 label=StoreCharacterTextPointer
D $EFB5 Stores a text pointer on the character being processed and clears bit 6 of its record. A non-zero return means the script step succeeded.
N $EFB5 Run by #R$CA64 after the display record at #R$EFB3, from the show-message commands at #R$EE3D and
. #R$EEBB.
  $EFB5,$08 Prepare pointer #N$07F0 and marker #N$10 for the character being processed.
  $EFBD,$03 Call #R$F1C1 to update that object.
  $EFC0,$04 Clear bit 6 of the character record.
  $EFC4,$02,b$01 Reset the zero flag.
  $EFC6,$01 Return.

b $EFC7 Display Record
D $EFC7 Display record read by #R$C9BF. The show-message commands at #R$EE46, #R$EEC3, #R$EEDB
. and #R$EF09 pass this word to #R$C591.
N $EFC7 Named from the script commands at #R$EE46, #R$EEC3, #R$EEDB and #R$EF09.
B $EFC7,$02 Display record read by #R$C9BF: flags #N$00, value #N$00.

c $EFC9 Match Sherlock Disguise
@ $EFC9 label=MatchSherlockDisguise
D $EFC9 Goes to the special-case object when Sherlock's disguise is one of seven ids.
N $EFC9 Run by #R$CA64 after the display record at #R$EFC7, from the show-message commands at #R$EE46,
. #R$EEC3, #R$EEDB and #R$EF09.
  $EFC9,$03 Read Sherlock's disguise.
  $EFCC,$04 Go to #R$EFE6 if the disguise is #N$23.
  $EFD0,$04 Go to #R$EFE6 if the disguise is #N$21.
  $EFD4,$04 Go to #R$EFE6 if the disguise is #N$22.
  $EFD8,$04 Go to #R$EFE6 if the disguise is #N$26.
  $EFDC,$04 Go to #R$EFE6 if the disguise is #N$25.
  $EFE0,$04 Go to #R$EFE6 if the disguise is #N$24.
  $EFE4,$02 See whether the disguise is #N$27.
  $EFE6,$03 Go to #R$DFCC if the disguise matched.
  $EFE9,$05 Clear the text pointer and use the marker #N$80.
  $EFEE,$03 Call #R$EFBA to update the character's object.
  $EFF1,$04 Set bit 6 of the character record.
  $EFF5,$01 Return.

