c $F19D Reject A Lower Character Id
@ $F19D label=RejectLowerCharacterId
D $F19D Returns zero when the character being processed is below the id passed in. A non-zero return means the script step succeeded.
  $F19D,$08 Return zero through #R$DC15 if the character being processed is below this id.
  $F1A5,$02,b$01 Reset the zero flag.
  $F1A7,$01 Return.

b $F1A8 Display Record
D $F1A8 Display record read by #R$C9BF. The show-message command at #R$F097 passes this word to
. #R$C591.
N $F1A8 Named from the script command at #R$F097.
B $F1A8,$02 Display record read by #R$C9BF: flags #N$00, value #N$00.

c $F1AA Print The Lower-Id Message
@ $F1AA label=RejectLowerCharacterId_PrintMessage
D $F1AA Prints the message and clears bit 6 of the character record. A non-zero return means the script step succeeded.
N $F1AA Run by #R$CA64 after the display record at #R$F1A8, from the show-message command at #R$F097.
  $F1AA,$03 Take the message at #R$6929+#N$0434.
  $F1AD,$05 Prepare the text pointer #N$0910 and the marker #N$20.
  $F1B2,$05 Call #R$F1C1 to update object #N$0B.
  $F1B7,$04 Clear bit 6 of the character record.
  $F1BB,$03 Call #R$A59F to print the message.
  $F1BE,$02,b$01 Reset the zero flag.
  $F1C0,$01 Return.

c $F1C1 Update Object Location
@ $F1C1 label=UpdateObjectLocation
D $F1C1 Looks the object up and stores the new location together with the low digit of its flags.
  $F1C1,$03 Call #R$D237 to look that object up.
  $F1C4,$06 Store the low byte of the text pointer and store the high byte of the text
. pointer.
  $F1CA,$06 Read the byte at offset #N$08, keep its low digit and fold in #REGb.
  $F1D0,$03 Store the new value at offset #N$08 of the record.
  $F1D3,$02,b$01 Reset the zero flag.
  $F1D5,$01 Return.

c $F1D6 Action: Room And Character Flags
@ $F1D6 label=ActionRoomAndCharacterFlags
D $F1D6 Checks the room, the clock and the current character, then sets or clears object
. flags for this action. A non-zero return means the script step succeeded.
. Reached through the table at #R$9FAB, read by #R$C583.
B $F1D6,$02 Display record read by #R$C9BF: flags #N$07, value #N$00.
N $F1D8 Run by #R$CA64 after the display record at #R$F1D6.
  $F1D8,$09 Take the morning marker and go to #R$F1E5 if the hour is below #N$0D.
  $F1E1,$04 Take the afternoon marker and subtract #N$0C to make the hour.
@ $F1E5 label=ActionRoomAndCharacterFlags_Next
  $F1E5,$07 Go to #R$DC15 if the hour does not match the clock at #R$9FE0.
  $F1EC,$07 Go to #R$DC15 if the AM/PM marker at #R$9FE2 does not match.
  $F1F3,$02,b$01 Reset the zero flag.
  $F1F5,$01 Return.
N $F1F6 Named from the script command at #R$EF0C.
B $F1F6,$02 Display record read by #R$C9BF: flags #N$07, value #N$00.
N $F1F8 Run by #R$CA64 after the display record at #R$F1F6.
  $F1F8,$08 Read the current object and mark the object-attribute flag.
  $F200,$02,b$01 Reset the zero flag.
  $F202,$01 Return.
B $F203,$02 Display record read by #R$C9BF: flags #N$07, value #N$00.
N $F205 Run by #R$CA64 after the display record at #R$F203.
  $F205,$08 Read the current object and clear bit 0 of its flags.
  $F20D,$02,b$01 Reset the zero flag.
  $F20F,$01 Return.
B $F210,$02 Display record read by #R$C9BF: flags #N$07, value #N$00.
N $F212 Run by #R$CA64 after the display record at #R$F210.
  $F212,$08 Read the current object and set bit 0 of its flags.
  $F21A,$02,b$01 Reset the zero flag.
  $F21C,$01 Return.
